<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
   xmlns:ns1="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#"
   xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
   xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
   xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEntity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nf8a41f19d11c4ce58930b9863d52190ab1"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The Transport Entity concept represents the identity of the circumscribed portion of energy or mass that is moved.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transport Entity</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
    <ns1:coversRequirements rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">What is the extent of a point source pollution event? Where did a voyage begin, and where did it end?</ns1:coversRequirements>
    <ns1:hasConsequences rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This CP allows data modellers and ontology creators the ability to filter and categorise large geoscience data stores.</ns1:hasConsequences>
    <ns1:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To reduce dimensionality of large data collections.</ns1:hasIntent>
    <ns1:relatedCPs rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">No known CPs at this time.</ns1:relatedCPs>
    <ns1:scenarios rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The rive water has pollution from a location, after a certain time.  A package left Auckland, New Zealand, at 5:45am on 01/06/2012 and arrived in Los Angeles, USA, on 01/12/2012.</ns1:scenarios>
    <rdfs:label>Transport Pattern</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">0.1</owl:versionInfo>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Created by Brandon Whitehead</owl:versionInfo>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nf8a41f19d11c4ce58930b9863d52190ab2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#partOf"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEvent"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nf8a41f19d11c4ce58930b9863d52190ab1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#partOf"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEvent"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#referenceFrame">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEvent"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEvent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>This property is significant in that it serves to restrict and disambiguate a myriad of inherent facets, often in juxtaposition, associated with the Earths complex phenomena. The reference frame is provided to restrict the input values for a given instantiation, inherently providing context to the local representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reference frame</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportMechanim">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nf8a41f19d11c4ce58930b9863d52190ab2"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The transportMechanism concept captures the nature of the source that acts upon the transportEntity, and thus induces a transportEvent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transport Mechanism</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#TransportEvent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Transport Event describes a specific transport phenomenon, as movement of some mass or energy (measurable entity) from one location to another, based on a common and persistent frame of reference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transport Event</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.descartes-core.org/patterns/owl/transportPattern#partOf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">part of</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
</rdf:RDF>
